# update vs devenv-stdlib pin

`update` / `devenv update` refresh **your** `devenv.lock`, then
`modules/non-nix/catalog.local.toml` (team tools: Nix if promotable, else
mise), then optional `update.local.sh`. Framework-shipped tools (Serena,
Headroom, MCP pins, debtmap, vendored `.agents/skills/`) move when you bump
the `devenv-stdlib` flake input.

```
# ❌ BAD — fighting the next pin bump
# modules/non-nix/catalog.toml
pin = "9.9.9"

# ✅ GOOD — team tools
# modules/non-nix/catalog.local.toml  (committed in the monorepo)
# then: update

# ✅ GOOD — framework pins
nix flake update devenv-stdlib
# or edit inputs.devenv-stdlib.url and refresh flake.lock
```

Do not edit shipped `modules/non-nix/catalog.toml` pins (or generated
`mise.toml`) to "upgrade" the stack. `devenv update` is the devenv CLI
(flake inputs). `update` is our script; it wraps that CLI in consumer mode.
